<title>EGYPT: Egyptian money supply grows 10.5 pct to Nov 96.</title>
<headline>Egyptian money supply grows 10.5 pct to Nov 96.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian broad money supply grew 10.5 percent in the year to the end of November 1996, from 10.3in the year to October and 10.4 to the end of November 1995, according to International Monetary Fund statistics.</p>
<p>Total money supply, including quasi-money and foreign currency deposits, was 178.642 billion pounds at the end of November, against 177.483 billion at the end of October.</p>
<p>				 Nov 96     Oct 96	Nov 95</p>
<p> Money			 44.595     44.841	41.190</p>
<p> Quasi-money		134.047    132.642     120.412</p>
<p> Total money supply     178.642    177.483     161.602</p>
<p>     Month-on-month	+0.65	+1.48	 +0.44</p>
<p>     Year-on-year	 +10.5	+10.3	 +10.4</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
